  "summary": "A modest, elaborate Japanese street fashion built on Rococo and Victorian silhouettes: bell skirts, petticoats, bows and lace — not related to the novel.",
  "description": "Emerging from 1980s street culture and brands like Baby, the Stars Shine Bright, Lolita fashion rejects both Western \"sexy\" norms and adult casualwear for an elaborate, deliberately modest dress-up: cupcake silhouettes over petticoats, knee socks, headdresses and parasols. Substyles include Gothic (Moi-même-Moitié), Sweet, Classic and Ouji. Practitioners emphasize craftsmanship, community etiquette and self-possession; it is Japan's most exported street fashion.",
